# Database Patterns (Drizzle ORM)

## Schema Definition
- Define schemas in `/src/db/schema/`
- Use snake_case for table and column names
- Group related tables in the same schema file
- Export types from schema using `$inferSelect` and `$inferInsert`
- Use appropriate data types (text, integer, boolean, timestamp, etc.)

Example:
```typescript
import { pgTable, text, integer, timestamp, uuid } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core"

export const capability = pgTable("capability", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  title: text("title").notNull(),
  slug: text("slug").notNull().unique(),
  description: text("description"),
  status: text("status").$type<"solved" | "partial" | "unsolved">(),
  progressPercentage: integer("progress_percentage").default(0),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
})

// Export types
export type Capability = typeof capability.$inferSelect
export type NewCapability = typeof capability.$inferInsert
```

## Relationships
- Use `references()` for foreign keys
- Define relations using `relations()` helper
- Use one-to-many and many-to-many patterns appropriately

Example:
```typescript
import { relations } from "drizzle-orm"

export const capabilityRelations = relations(capability, ({ one, many }) => ({
  category: one(capabilityCategory, {
    fields: [capability.categoryId],
    references: [capabilityCategory.id],
  }),
  bottlenecks: many(bottleneck),
  predictions: many(capabilityPrediction),
}))
```

## Querying
- Use Drizzle's query builder (type-safe)
- Use `.with()` for eager loading related data
- Implement pagination with `limit()` and `offset()`
- Use `.$dynamic()` for conditional query building
- Return only needed columns with `.select()`

Example:
```typescript
import { db } from "@/db"
import { capability, capabilityCategory } from "@/db/schema"
import { eq, desc } from "drizzle-orm"

// Basic query
const capabilities = await db
  .select()
  .from(capability)
  .where(eq(capability.status, "partial"))
  .orderBy(desc(capability.createdAt))
  .limit(20)

// Query with relations
const capabilityWithCategory = await db.query.capability.findFirst({
  where: eq(capability.id, id),
  with: {
    category: true,
    bottlenecks: true,
  },
})

// Conditional query building
const query = db.select().from(capability).$dynamic()

if (status) {
  query.where(eq(capability.status, status))
}

const results = await query
```

## Mutations
- Use transactions for multi-table operations
- Use `.returning()` to get inserted/updated data
- Validate input with Zod before inserting
- Handle unique constraint violations

Example:
```typescript
// Insert
const [newCapability] = await db
  .insert(capability)
  .values({
    title: "New capability",
    slug: "new-capability",
  })
  .returning()

// Update
const [updated] = await db
  .update(capability)
  .set({ status: "solved" })
  .where(eq(capability.id, id))
  .returning()

// Delete
await db
  .delete(capability)
  .where(eq(capability.id, id))

// Transaction
await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
  const [capability] = await tx
    .insert(capability)
    .values(capabilityData)
    .returning()

  await tx
    .insert(bottleneck)
    .values({
      capabilityId: capability.id,
      type: "hardware",
    })
})
```

## Migrations
- Generate migrations: `bun run db:generate`
- Run migrations: `bun run db:migrate`
- Review generated SQL before applying
- Never edit migrations manually after they're applied
- Keep migrations in version control

## Database Connection
- Use Neon serverless driver for PostgreSQL
- Connection is configured in `/src/db/index.ts`
- Connection string from `DATABASE_URL` environment variable
- HTTP-based connection (no connection pooling overhead)

Example:
```typescript
import { neon } from "@neondatabase/serverless"
import { drizzle } from "drizzle-orm/neon-http"
import * as schema from "./schema"

const sql = neon(process.env.DATABASE_URL!)
export const db = drizzle(sql, { schema })
```

## Best Practices
- Use prepared statements for repeated queries
- Index frequently queried columns
- Avoid N+1 queries (use eager loading with `.with()`)
- Use database constraints (unique, not null, foreign keys)
- Set appropriate default values
- Use timestamps (createdAt, updatedAt) for audit trails
- Consider using database-generated UUIDs for primary keys

## Performance Tips
- Use `.select()` to limit returned columns
- Implement pagination for large datasets
- Use indexes on foreign keys and frequently filtered columns
- Consider using database views for complex queries
- Monitor query performance with Drizzle Studio (`bun run db:studio`)

## Enums
- Define enums using PostgreSQL enum types or text with type casting
- Export enum values as TypeScript types
- Use in Zod schemas for validation

Example:
```typescript
import { pgEnum } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core"

export const capabilityStatusEnum = pgEnum("capability_status", [
  "solved",
  "partial",
  "unsolved",
])

export const capability = pgTable("capability", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  status: capabilityStatusEnum("status").default("unsolved"),
})
```
